# verdict: unsatisfiable
# Source: ty mdtest type_properties/implies_subtype_of.md:1174
#   Constraint implication / Transitivity / Transitivity should not introduce
#   impossible constraints
# ty: (int <= A <= T | U) and (T <= str) implies (int <= U). Adding
# (U <= bytes) makes the constraint set unsatisfiable.
#
# The unit states constraint sets over type variables directly, so each type
# variable is a metavariable and each bound is one assertion. The upper bound
# of A is a union of two metavariables, so int must reach T or U through A.
# The bound on T blocks the T arm, and the bound on U blocks the U arm. Without
# `u_upper` the input is satisfiable, and int must go to U. That is the
# implication that the unit checks. The core needs all four assertions.
class int;
class str;
class bytes;
metavar ?A;
metavar ?T;
metavar ?U;

assert a_lower: int <: ?A;
assert a_upper: ?A <: ?T | ?U;
assert t_upper: ?T <: str;
assert u_upper: ?U <: bytes;
